  "body": "## What and why\n\nFollow-up remainder of #557 (filed by triage task 11869, lane code-u, 2026-11-07). Two of #557's three acceptance criteria are landed and verified at main `801ceb9cb1`:\n\n- Per-world total memory budget with refusal tests — PR #4628 merged 2026-11-03 (design PR #3877).\n- Idle-eviction checkpoint/reopen integrity under load — the `many_worlds` measurement record shows checkpoints=100, evicted=100, reopened=100 with sequence/records asserted (`pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md`, \"Many-worlds scale measurement (#557, F11.8 remainder)\").\n\nThe one unmet criterion is performance. The F11.8 `many_worlds` workload (1,000 durable idle worlds + 100 leased active worlds, 20 ev/s per active world, 10 s, 20,000 commands; `pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs` `bench_many_worlds`) was measured on the reference machine on 2026-11-02 and recorded in `pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt:14`:\n\n```text\nbench many_worlds unit=ms_per_command median=1076.753 min=6.368 reps=1 p50_ms=1076.753 p95_ms=4547.595 p99_ms=5650.792 target_p99_ms=50 target_met=false idle_worlds=1000 active_worlds=100 events_per_second=20 duration_secs=10 commands=20000 load_elapsed_secs=13.132 completed_events_per_second=1523.1 checkpoint_triggers=100 checkpoints=100 evicted=100 reopened=100\n```\n\np99 is 5,650.792 ms against the 50 ms target (~113× over), and completed throughput was 1,523.1/s against the scheduled 2,000/s. Nobody has yet profiled where the submission-to-acknowledgement latency accumulates.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A profiling record (on the implementing PR or this issue) names the dominant phase of the many_worlds submission-to-acknowledgement latency with measured evidence\n- [ ] A scoped fix for that phase lands with tests; existing pkgs/id tests stay green (CI)\n- [ ] The many_worlds bench is re-run on the reference machine and the new line is recorded in `pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt` and `pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md` with the p99 delta vs 5,650.792 ms\n- [ ] If p99 remains above 50 ms, the remaining gap and the next identified phase are recorded here and on #557; #557 closes only on a recorded `target_met=true` run\n\n## Scope notes\n\n- Do not redo the landed memory-budget work (PR #4628) or the eviction-integrity assertions.\n- Do not change the 50 ms target or the workload shape to make the target pass.\n- Why a separate issue: the canonical queue dedupe key `repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:557` is consumed by done task 7502, whose scope explicitly excluded p99 latency optimization — a fix packet for the remainder under that key is a dedupe-blocked orphan. This issue carries the remainder so its fix packet (task enqueued with this issue) is live and claimable. #557 remains the parent tracker.\n\n## Links\n\n- Parent: #557\n- Prerequisite harness: #539 (F11.8 benchmark harness)\n- Evidence: `pkgs/id/benches/BASELINES.md`, `pkgs/id/benches/baseline.txt:14`, `pkgs/id/benches/world_bench.rs`\n",
